{"id":"b12cc9634756eb6e425c24c05e568473e4cf608e","axis":"silent","repo":"aquasecurity/trivy","sha":"b12cc9634756eb6e425c24c05e568473e4cf608e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/guide/coverage/language/golang.md","lines":["@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ On the other hand, it uses `go.mod` for direct dependencies and `go.sum` for ind"," Go 1.17+ holds actually needed indirect dependencies in `go.mod`, and it reduces false detection."," `go.sum` in Go 1.16 or less contains all indirect dependencies that are even not needed for compiling."," If you want to have better detection, please consider updating the Go version in your project.","-See [go.sum](#gomod-gosum) for why `go.sum` is skipped in Go 1.17+ projects.","+See [go.sum](#gomod-gosum) for why Trivy does not take dependencies from `go.sum` in Go 1.17+ projects."," "," !!! note","     The Go version doesn't mean your Go tool version, but the Go version in your go.mod.","@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ See [go.sum](#gomod-gosum) for why `go.sum` is skipped in Go 1.17+ projects.","     ```"," "," ### go.sum { #gomod-gosum }","-Trivy skips `go.sum` in Go 1.17+ projects, because it lists more modules than the build uses.","+In Go 1.17+ projects, Trivy does not take dependencies from `go.sum`, because it lists more modules than the build uses. Trivy still reads `go.sum` for [module checksums](#module-checksums)."," "," A common extra entry is a module that another module needs to run its own tests. Go keeps such a module out of `go.mod` and never compiles it into your binary, so a vulnerability in it does not affect your project. Your own tests are a different case. Their dependencies are listed in `go.mod`, and Trivy reports them."," ","@@ -130,6 +130,24 @@ Trivy detects the Go version used to compile the binary and detects its vulnerab"," It possibly produces false positives."," See [the caveat](#stdlib-vulnerabilities) for details."," ","+## Module Checksums","+Trivy records the h1 checksum of a Go module as a SHA-256 digest of the package with the `go-module-h1` source. For a replaced module, Trivy reports the replacement and its checksum. The h1 checksum is a SHA-256 hash over the list of the module files and their SHA-256 hashes, so it does not match the SHA-256 of the module zip file. See [go.sum files](https://go.dev/ref/mod#go-sum-files) for details.","+","+For Go modules, Trivy takes the checksum from the `go.sum` file next to `go.mod`. A module gets no checksum if `go.sum` has only its `/go.mod` line, because that line covers only the `go.mod` file of the module.","+","+For Go binaries, Trivy takes the checksum from the build info. A module replaced with a local directory has no checksum. The main module has a checksum only if the binary was built with `go install module@version`.","+","+Trivy does not verify the checksums against the [checksum database](https://go.dev/ref/mod#checksum-database) or the module contents.","+","+To compare a digest with the h1 form that Go uses, convert the hex value to base64 and add the `h1:` prefix. Then compare it with the line in `go.sum` or with the `Sum` field from `go mod download -json`.","+","+```","+$ echo 828d5b2bf0ff045655d88f1c21077534a119fb4a304931b57c34dc8b822a15c1 | xxd -r -p | base64","+go1bK/D/BFZV2I8cIQd1NKEZ+0owSTG1fDTci4IqFcE=","+$ go mod download -json golang.org/x/xerrors@v0.0.0-20200804184101-5ec99f83aff1 | jq -r .Sum","+h1:go1bK/D/BFZV2I8cIQd1NKEZ+0owSTG1fDTci4IqFcE=","+```","+"," ## Caveats"," "," ### Stdlib Vulnerabilities"],"additions":20,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"integration/integration_test.go","lines":["@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@ const ("," \tgoldenDockerfileFilePattern                  = \"testdata/dockerfile_file_pattern.json.golden\""," \tgoldenDotNet                                 = \"testdata/dotnet.json.golden\""," \tgoldenGoMod                                  = \"testdata/gomod.json.golden\"","+\tgoldenGoModCycloneDX                         = \"testdata/gomod-cyclonedx.json.golden\""," \tgoldenGoModSkip                              = \"testdata/gomod-skip.json.golden\""," \tgoldenGoModVEX                               = \"testdata/gomod-vex.json.golden\""," \tgoldenGradle                                 = \"testdata/gradle.json.golden\""],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"integration/repo_test.go","lines":["@@ -478,6 +478,15 @@ func TestRepository(t *testing.T) {"," \t\t\t},"," \t\t\tgolden: goldenCondaEnvironmentCycloneDX,"," \t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"gomod generating CycloneDX SBOM\",","+\t\t\targs: repoTestArgs{","+\t\t\t\tcommand: \"fs\",","+\t\t\t\tformat:  \"cyclonedx\",","+\t\t\t\tinput:   \"testdata/fixtures/repo/gomod\",","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\tgolden: goldenGoModCycloneDX,","+\t\t},"," \t\t{"," \t\t\tname: \"pom.xml generating CycloneDX SBOM (with vulnerabilities)\","," \t\t\targs: repoTestArgs{"],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"integration/testdata/gomod-cyclonedx.json.golden","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,1147 @@","+{","+  \"$schema\": \"http://cyclonedx.org/schema/bom-1.7.schema.json\",","+  \"bomFormat\": \"CycloneDX\",","+  \"specVersion\": \"1.7\",","+  \"serialNumber\": \"urn:uuid:3ff14136-e09f-4df9-80ea-000000000041\",","+  \"version\": 1,","+  \"metadata\": {","+    \"timestamp\": \"2021-08-25T12:20:30+00:00\",","+    \"tools\": {","+      \"components\": [","+        {","+          \"type\": \"application\",","+          \"manufacturer\": {","+            \"name\": \"Aqua Security Software Ltd.\"","+          },","+          \"group\": \"aquasecurity\",","+          \"name\": \"trivy\",","+          \"version\": \"dev\"","+        }","+      ]","+    },","+    \"component\": {","+      \"bom-ref\": \"3ff14136-e09f-4df9-80ea-000000000002\",","+      \"type\": \"application\",","+      \"name\": \"testdata/fixtures/repo/gomod\",","+      \"properties\": [","+        {","+          \"name\": \"aquasecurity:trivy:SchemaVersion\",","+          \"value\": \"2\"","+        }","+      ]","+    }","+  },","+  \"components\": ["